<title>GERMANY: European merger should counter Boeing - Kohl.</title>
<headline>European merger should counter Boeing - Kohl.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Chancellor Helmut Kohl on Friday urged European aerospace firms to consolidate in response to the competitive threat from the planned merger of Boeing Co with McDonnell Douglas Co.</p>
<p>&quot;I think that Europe must give a very clear answer to the American challenge in the aerospace sector by founding its own large concern,&quot; Kohl told a news conference.  </p>
<p>The European Commission is expected next week to block the $14 billion merger, after concessions by Boeing failed to allay fears in Brussels that the merged U.S. entity would unfairly dominate the European aircraft market.</p>
<p>Kohl added: &quot;I am for a merger. I want to bring together the Europeans in the next few years.&quot; He said he would call a cabinet meeting this autumn to discuss the matter.</p>
<p>Germany supports plans by Boeing's main competitor, the European Airbus Industrie consortium, to press ahead with plans to create a limited-liability company by 1999.</p>
<p>Airbus groups Germany's Daimler-Benz Aerospace AG, British Aerospace, France's Aerospatiale and CASA of Spain.</p>
